Z||000000||speed racer||03-28-2001||06:32 PM||||How do you guys think my v-6 would sound with no cat. and a flowmaster 40 series. I might even add headers tell me what you think I should do and how they both would sound.<BR>Thanks<BR>Kyle <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||RiceCooker||03-28-2001||06:50 PM||||Since that's exactly what i have i'll tell you<P>VERY LOUD and throaty<P>I have flowmaster, no cat, 2 1/4" piping and fierostore sprint headers. <P>People tell me all the time it sounds like a V8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>The only thing i don't like is that on the highway it is very loud because my car is only a 4 spd and the RPM's are high.<BR>It sounds sooooo mean when you revv it to 4,000 and let it come down. You might get annoyed if you don't have a good stereo because you don't want it to be loud all the time.<P>Any other questions just ask<BR>Todd <P>------------------<BR>Kids in the back seat cause accidents<BR>Accidents in the back seat cause kids||||reg||6
Z||000002||stimpy||03-28-2001||06:55 PM||||I have a Flowmaster with a Random Tech. low restriction cat. It sounds nasty. Makes neat burbling sounds at idle, then shrieks at high RPM. Cool little "backfire" popping on deceleration. Sounds very racy. Getting headers just for the sound seems a bit overkill,but hey, it's your bucks.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||03-28-2001||07:24 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/Exh_gif/Flowell_Left_200_low.jpg"> <P>if you decide to go with headers we have both long tube and short tube headers to choose from, as well as a re-designed Flowmaster muffler to fit specifically into a Fiero. Also with the Flowmaster we carry Spintech mufflers as well. Spintech has won us over here at the shop as they provide a very deep rumble, but not as obnoxious as the Flowmaster. If you have any questions give us a ring.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
